// CotSC localization Batch 23: QCHIMTR
@1 = ~This is... this is Candlekeep? It's so... wrong. What is going on here, <CHARNAME>?~
@2 = ~I don't know, Imoen. We should keep moving. Try to see what we're up against.~
@3 = ~Why do you ask me? Do I look like a sage with all the answers?~
@4 = ~I may sound silly, but part of me was hoping old Winthrop was here with his usual greeting: 'You're late, you little viper.' Heh. He could always cheer me up.~
@5 = ~This place looks so decayed. Corrupted.~
@6 = ~Let's keep moving.~
@7 = ~He... he looked like...~
@8 = ~Dreppin. Yeah... I know.~
@9 = ~I don't want to think about it. Let's just go.~
@10 = ~Yeah, you're right. You're right. Let's just... deal with this as soon as possible.~
@11 = ~I know, I know. I'm just trying not to lose my head. I don't like the look of this. Let's just deal with this as quickly as we can.~
@12 = ~It's a pure nightmare. Why would your mind distort this place so badly? Do you think it's because... you know... you're a Child of Bhaal? Maybe our presence warps this place more than a normal person's would.~
@13 = ~I don't know, but if that is the case, I hope there is no worse danger here than those undead we encountered.~
@14 = ~I don't know. Let's just keep going.~
@15 = ~Yeah... I sure hope so. Let's go.~
@16 = ~What kind of madness is this? Remember when we came back to Candlekeep? Doppelgangers had taken over the whole place, and we found out about your origins for the first time. Things were bad enough then, but... at least our home didn't look as if it had been sucked into the Nine Hells, right? We have to find this core so we can leave.~
